# Infra & DevOps Conventions

Showcase infra: get it running reliably and reproducibly, don't gold-plate.

## Local environment

- **SQLite is the default DB** — zero-config, single file at
  `database/database.sqlite`. Plain `php artisan serve` + SQLite; no DB server.
  `touch database/database.sqlite` then migrate. Docker/Sail is optional — don't
  force it on the team.
- One command to a fresh demo DB: `php artisan migrate:fresh --seed`. Provide a
  `composer`/Makefile shortcut alongside `npm run dev` (Vite) and serve.
- Commit a **`.env.example`** with every key the app needs. Never commit real
  `.env` / secrets.

## Showcase host-laptop setup (LOCKED)

The showcase runs off **one host laptop** that serves the dashboard on the
projector; the other agents enter data from their own laptops over the LAN.

- Host runs Laravel bound to all interfaces:
  `php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000`.
- Agents open `http://<host-ip>:8000` (find it with `ip addr` / `hostname -I`).
- SQLite file lives on the host only — all writes go through the host's Laravel,
  so there's no shared-file-locking problem; agents just use the web app.
- Ensure Vite assets are built (`npm run build`) or the dev server is reachable;
  confirm session cookies + CSRF work for the LAN origin, not just `localhost`.
- Everyone on the **same wifi/hotspot**. Test the LAN round-trip before the demo,
  not during it. Have the host laptop's IP written down.

## "Live" = polling (LOCKED)

No websockets/Reverb. The dashboard and live list poll every ~2–3s via Inertia
`router.reload({ only: [...] })`. Nothing to run beyond the web server — that's
the point: it survives flaky venue wifi.

## Config, not env(), in app code

Read config through `config/*.php` and reference `config('...')` in code. Calling
`env()` outside config breaks `config:cache`.

## Demo-reliability checklist

- **Pre-seed all data** (agents, markets, a realistic spread of reports with a few
  outliers) so nothing external is on the critical path during judging.
- `migrate:fresh --seed` must produce a demo-ready DB every time.
- Have a **known-good reset**: if entries get messy mid-practice, re-seed in one
  command.
- The dashboard must render fine with thin data — "collecting data / low
  confidence", never a crash or blank tile.
- Voice is parked (`030`) — no mic/provider dependencies on the critical path.

## Deployment (only if you actually deploy instead of host-laptop)

A single small VM or Forge/Fly/Render is plenty: `config:cache`, `route:cache`,
`migrate --force`, build Vite assets. A stable host-laptop demo beats a shaky
deploy — only do this if the team explicitly wants a shared URL.
